    "doc_text": "XIN_ENG_20061107.0274\n\nQINGDAO, Nov. 7 , 2006 (Xinhua)\n\nPhilippines\n\n\n\n\nA fleet of the Chinese People's Liberation Army (PLA) Navy ended a 79-day voyage and arrived this port city in east China's Shandong Province on Tuesday, after visiting four ports in the United States, Canada and the Philippines.\n\nAt 10:00 am, a grand ceremony was held at the Navy port, to welcome the fleet, composing the missile destroyer, \"Qingdao\", and the depot ship, \"Lake Hongze\", with 506 officers and men on board.\n\nOn Aug. 21, the fleet left Qingdao Port, since then, it traveled 17,000 sea miles and successfully passed through three typhonic centers.\n\nDuring the journey, Chinese and the U.S. navy held their first joint maritime exercise.",
